{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"4a039a7b-a04d-4c6d-a6f3-551b98e415f4","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have identified the causes of the silent failure, fixed the configuration and script, and documented the details in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-KNSAZt/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Causes \u0026 Fixes\n1. **Missing `USER` environment variable in launchd (`Not logged in · Please run /login`)**:\n   - [launchctl-print.txt](file:///tmp/h-KNSAZt/launchctl-print.txt) showed the job ran 6 times (`runs = 6`) with `last exit code = 1`, and [nightly-review.err](file:///tmp/h-KNSAZt/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err) logged `Not logged in · Please run /login` on every run because `USER` was not set in `EnvironmentVariables`, preventing `claude` from finding its login in the macOS Keychain.\n   - **Fix**: Added `\u003ckey\u003eUSER\u003c/key\u003e\u003cstring\u003evk\u003c/string\u003e` to `EnvironmentVariables` in [com.vk.nightly-review.plist](file:///tmp/h-KNSAZt/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist#L23-L30).\n\n2. **Assigning to read-only `status` in `zsh` (`read-only variable: status`)**:\n   - Line 19 of [nightly-review.zsh](file:///tmp/h-KNSAZt/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L18-L28) assigned `status=$?`. Because `status` is a read-only special variable in `zsh`, the shell immediately aborted on line 19 before reaching [notify.sh](file:///tmp/h-KNSAZt/bin/notify.sh).\n   - **Fix**: Replaced `status=$?` with `rc=$?`, piped the multi-line prompt to `claude -p` via stdin (`print -r -- \"$PROMPT\" | claude -p ...`) so stdin is cleanly closed after the prompt, added a check that `$OUT` is non-empty (`[ ! -s \"$OUT\" ]`), and logged run duration (`${SECONDS}s`).\n","duration_seconds":88.365837,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":31333,"output_tokens":3301,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":90524,"total_tokens":34634}}}
